94
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:50,080
would be directed by you,

95
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:52,340
that you'd give us wisdom to hear from you

96
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:56,000
and wisdom to understand what is next for our church.

97
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,720
Pray for this incredible provision

98
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:00,400
for our church in this next season.

99
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,200
And God, pray for this message.

100
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,760
Pray that your Holy Spirit would be present

101
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:07,100
and active in the lives of everyone

102
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:08,520
that's listening to this message.

103
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:10,340
I pray that we would hear specifically

104
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:13,440
from you this morning for your glory and our good.

105
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,320
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

106
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,160
Amen.

107
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:19,040
Well, like I said at the beginning,

108
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:22,720
this is our fourth week of this series on deconstruction.

109
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:25,460
And last week, Pastor Brandon covered the story

110
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:28,060
of Nicodemus coming to Jesus at night

111
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:31,640
with questions about how to reconcile his religion,

112
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:35,560
this religious system that he'd grown up in his entire life,

113
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:37,320
the system that he gave his life to,

114
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:40,060
this system that he was kind of working in.

115
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:43,260
It was his profession and the God that he grew up hearing about

116
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,960
and learning about and hearing stories about.

117
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:47,580
He was trying to reconcile not only the stories

118
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:48,340
he'd heard about God,

119
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:51,160
but seeing God in the flesh in front of him,

120
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:53,060
being able to interact and have conversations

121
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:55,020
with God in the flesh.

122
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:58,100
And he was trying to reconcile his religion

123
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:01,780
and what he knew to be true about God.

124
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:03,820
And that's kind of been the overarching application

125
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:06,140
as we've talked about this idea

126
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:09,100
of deconstruction and faith renovation.

127
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:11,700
As we've said, people that are both

128
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:13,900
kind of rebelling against God

129
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:16,440
and people who are entrenched in a religious system

130
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:20,720
both need to tear down some of their previously held beliefs

131
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:24,660
in order to better understand the heart of the Father.

132
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,680
I think that's the beautiful thing about Canvas

133
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:30,180
is we have people on all different sides of the spectrum.

134
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:32,540
We have people that are just now coming to church

135
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:34,520
to ask questions about Jesus.

136
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:37,140
We have people that are kind of have been running away

137
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:38,160
from God for a long time.

138
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:39,580
We have people who have grown up in the church

139
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:40,880
and been in church their whole lives.

140
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:43,700
And I think it's important for all of us

141
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:45,780
to find common ground and unity

142
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:49,120
as we seek to better understand the heart of the Father.

143
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,900
That's the goal of this entire series,

144
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:55,680
that we would better understand the heart of the Father.

145
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,540
So we said that from the outset,

146
00:05:57,540 --> 00:06:00,480
and that's going to continue to be our goal this morning.

147
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:01,280
If you have your Bibles,

148
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:04,260
I'd love to have you turn to Genesis chapter 3.

149
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:06,580
We're going to be in Genesis chapter 3 and 4,

150
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:09,540
and then we'll hop over to Matthew 4 at the end.

151
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:12,040
As you're turning, I was really struggling

152
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,820
with how to introduce this message,

153
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:16,880
how to get into our topic for this morning.

154
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:18,860
And this morning I was listening to,

155
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:21,360
or earlier this week I was listening to a podcast,

156
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,620
and he made this statement.

157
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:27,580
He said that oftentimes the goal of science

158
00:06:27,580 --> 00:06:30,000
is to disprove science.

159
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,620
And so science is built on theories.

160
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:34,820
It's built on hypothesis.

161
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,640
It's built on these conditional statements

162
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:38,420
where scientists start out with a hypothesis,

163
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:41,980
and they say if this reacts this way,

164
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:43,340
then this must be true, right?

165
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:44,840
There's these conditional statements

166
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:48,080
that they're trying to prove based on theories they have.

167
00:06:48,100 --> 00:06:50,060
And then once a theory is proven,

168
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:53,800
it's held as the proven theory

169
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,440
until another scientist comes along

170
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:57,720
and disproves that theory.

171
00:06:57,720 --> 00:07:00,940
So we have these conditional if-then statements.

172
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:02,860
The biggest one that I can think of

173
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:04,980
that growing up affected me in my childhood

174
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:06,260
is Pluto, right?

175
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:08,260
Like a lot of you grew up being taught

176
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:09,400
that Pluto was a planet,

177
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:12,080
and then other scientists with other information

178
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:14,500
came along and realized maybe Pluto is not a planet.

179
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,100
And then more scientists came along with more information,

180
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,740
and now I think it might be a planet again.

181
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:22,060
I tried to find the answer on the internet this week

182
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:23,620
and really couldn't figure out

183
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:25,320
if it is or is not a planet.

184
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:29,520
But really, we have a lot of these conditional statements

185
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:30,980
in our life, right?

186
00:07:30,980 --> 00:07:33,420
If this happens, then this will happen.

187
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:35,240
If I do this, then this will happen.

188
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:39,080
And I came up with a couple of examples

189
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:43,100
that I think might help us hop into this.

190
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:44,940
So here's one.

191
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:47,400
If I go to work and I do a good job,

192
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,200
then I will get paid, right?

193
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:50,300
That's a conditional statement

194
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:52,200
that a lot of us base our life on.

195
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:54,060
If I go to work, I do a good job,

196
00:07:54,060 --> 00:07:54,940
I'll get a paycheck.

197
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:55,920
How about this one?

198
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,920
If I buy a Peloton,

199
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:01,420
I will definitely use it enough to justify the expense.

200
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:03,800
If I make this purchase,

201
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,360
I'm definitely going to use it enough

202
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:09,220
to make it worth my purchase price, right?

203
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:11,320
Some of us have Pelotons, and we use it plenty.

204
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:15,040
Some of us have Pelotons, and it is just a very expensive closet

205
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,900
that we put our coats on.

206
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:20,020
If I go to college, I'll get a good job, right?

207
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:22,720
That's a conditional statement that used to be really true,

208
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:24,860
and nowadays, maybe not so much.

209
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:27,180
A lot of you probably have lots of student debt,

210
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:29,680
and your college degree is just a piece of paper

211
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:31,180
that you could use as a napkin,

212
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:33,380
because there are no jobs, right?

213
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:35,620
If I have kids, they'll get older,

214
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:38,460
and they'll be able to help me with chores.

215
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:41,340
Some of you have kids, and you thought,

216
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:43,180
man, once they get older, they'll mow the lawn,

217
00:08:43,180 --> 00:08:43,920
they'll do the dishes.

218
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:46,580
But I've talked to some of you teenagers,

219
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:49,480
and that's not how it works.

220
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:53,020
So our life is built on these conditional statements, right?

221
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:57,480
We make decisions based on what we think the outcomes will be.

222
00:08:57,480 --> 00:09:00,960
If X happens, then Y will happen.

223
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:03,120
And I think if we're honest with ourselves,

224
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:05,080
when it comes to our faith and our religion

225
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:07,300
and our beliefs about God and the Bible,

226
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:12,280
I think sometimes we begin to believe

227
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:15,040
these false conditional statements about God

228
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:16,700
and the Bible and religion,

229
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:19,320
and we build our faith, and we build our religion

230
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:22,820
on what I would like to call conditional theologies,

231
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:25,280
false conditional theologies.

232
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:29,020
If I do X, then Y will happen.

233
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:32,840
And when the false equation fails us, we blame God.

234
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:35,100
We get mad at God because it didn't work out

235
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:37,980
the way that we thought it was going to work out.

236
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:39,820
I think a big contributing factor

237
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:43,080
to many of us deconstructing parts of our faith

238
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:46,420
is that we've bought into a false conditional theology.

239
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:49,920
We believe that if I do this, if I think this way,

240
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:52,860
if I chase after this, then this will be the outcome.

241
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:54,840
And then when that outcome doesn't work out,

242
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:57,560
we get mad at God because we blame Him

243
00:09:57,560 --> 00:10:00,480
for not holding up His end of the deal.

244
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:03,220
And so as we jump into our text in Genesis 3

245
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:05,160
and Genesis 4 this morning,

246
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:07,600
I want to unpack the conditional theology

247
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:12,040
of both the rebellious and the religious.

248
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,860
I think there's these conditional statements

249
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:16,660
that the people who are kind of walking away

250
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:18,580
from the faith, who are rebelling against God,

251
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:21,240
I think they're believing a specific lie,

252
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:23,960
a specific conditional theology that isn't true.

253
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:25,860
And on the other side of the coin,

254
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:27,940
I think there's people here that are entrenched

255
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:30,440
in a religious system, and they're basing their life

256
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:35,000
on a conditional theology of religion that also isn't true.

257
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,320
I want to kind of unpack those and help us understand

258
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:39,180
how I think they're impacting

259
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:42,480
some of our deconstruction process.

260
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:45,880
So Genesis chapter 3, starting in verse 1,

261
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:47,980
a lot of us are going to be familiar with this passage.

262
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:48,680
Let's check it out.

263
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:48,920
It says,

264
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:52,160
The serpent was the shrewdest of all the wild animals

265
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:53,480
the Lord God had made.

266
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:55,300
One day he asked the woman,

267
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:58,220
Did God really say to you that you must not eat the fruit

268
00:10:58,220 --> 00:10:59,820
from any of the trees in the garden?

269
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:01,380
Eve said,

270
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:03,400
Of course we may eat from the fruit of the trees

271
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:04,200
in the garden.

272
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:04,900
The woman replied,

273
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:06,960
It's only the fruit from the tree

274
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,160
in the middle of the garden

275
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:09,740
that we are not allowed to eat.

276
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:10,440
God said,

277
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:12,700
We must not eat it or even touch it.

278
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:14,900
If we do, we will die.

279
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:16,320
The enemy said,

280
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,260
You won't die.

281
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:19,760
God knows that your eyes will be opened

282
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:20,860
as soon as you eat it,

283
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:22,180
and you will be like God,

284
00:11:22,180 --> 00:11:24,340
knowing both good and evil.

285
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:25,180
Verse 6,

286
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:27,220
The woman was convinced.

287
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:30,300
She saw that the tree was beautiful

288
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:32,200
and that its fruit looked delicious,

289
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:34,440
and she wanted the wisdom it would give her.

290
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:36,920
So she took some fruit and she ate it.

291
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:39,480
Then she gave to her husband who was with her,

292
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:40,360
and he ate it too.

293
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:41,240
At that moment,

294
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:43,040
their eyes were opened,

295
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:45,680
and they suddenly felt shame at their nakedness,

296
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:47,340
so they sewed fig leaves together

297
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:49,480
to cover themselves.

298
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:52,020
So we have Adam and Eve in the garden,

299
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:53,860
literally living what I would say

300
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:56,060
is the ideal Christian life.

301
00:11:56,060 --> 00:11:57,160
They're in paradise.

302
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:58,180
They're in the Garden of Eden

303
00:11:58,180 --> 00:12:01,080
with everything that they could ever imagine,

304
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:04,660
with a perfect fellowship between them and God,

305
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:06,160
that God would literally meet them

306
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,460
and walk with them.

307
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,860
They were obeying all of the laws

308
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:10,920
that God had commanded them

309
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:13,480
because God literally only commanded them one law.

310
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,940
They had it so good, right?

311
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:17,600
They were living in right fellowship with God.

312
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:20,820
They were naked and together in paradise.

313
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:23,120
Sounds like a pretty good life.

314
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:25,400
And this is where they find themselves,

315
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:27,460
in right relationship with God,

316
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:29,200
in right relationship with one another,

317
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:32,440
literally in what we would probably call paradise.

318
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:35,420
And then temptation, the enemy,

319
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:38,040
temptation steps in and offers them

320
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:41,380
a conditional theology for the rebellious heart.

321
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:43,620
See, where they find themselves

322
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:45,140
is in right relationship with God,

323
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:46,420
in fellowship with God.

324
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:49,180
Everything is as it should be.

325
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:51,380
And then temptation comes in and says,

326
00:12:51,380 --> 00:12:53,360
what if you're missing out on something?

327
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:56,220
What if God's holding something back from you?

328
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:58,220
What if there's a better life for you to live?

329
00:12:58,220 --> 00:13:00,120
I know this life seems really great.

330
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:02,680
You've got your spouse and you're both naked

331
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:04,040
and you're in the Garden of Eden

332
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:04,920
and everything's great

333
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:06,920
and you have a perfect relationship with God.

334
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:09,860
But what if God's holding something back from you?

335
00:13:09,860 --> 00:13:12,240
See, if you eat this fruit,

336
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:14,920
you will become like God.

337
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,980
You'll have the one thing that you don't have.

338
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:19,240
God's holding back something from you.

339
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:20,620
And I'm telling you,

340
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:22,860
there's this different theology that you can believe.

341
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:25,700
That if you would just participate in these things

342
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:28,060
that look good, taste good, smell good, feel good,

343
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:30,600
then you'll be happy and you'll be satisfied.

344
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:33,880
And after one temptation from the enemy,

345
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:37,240
Eve's rebellious heart was convinced.

346
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:39,440
How was she convinced?

347
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:41,080
Look in verse six.

348
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:43,500
It says the woman was convinced she saw

349
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,160
that the tree was beautiful

350
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:46,660
and its fruit looked delicious

351
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:49,560
and she wanted the wisdom that it would give her.

352
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:52,560
See, I think this is the conditional theology

353
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:53,640
of the rebellious heart.

354
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:56,160
The conditional theology of the rebellious heart says,

355
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:59,580
if it looks good, tastes good, sounds good, feels good,

356
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:02,640
then it must be good for me to pursue

357
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:05,120
and or encourage others to pursue

358
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:08,040
without boundaries or limitations.

359
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:12,080
This is the conditional theology of the rebellious heart.

360
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:14,580
If it looks good, if it feels good,

361
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:16,080
if it makes me feel good,

362
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:17,480
then I'm going to pursue it

363
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:20,320
and nobody can tell me anything other than that.

364
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:22,400
I don't care what God says.

365
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:24,200
I care what I see.

366
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:27,380
And man, I see this so much in our culture today.

367
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:29,900
There's so much of this conditional theology

368
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:32,540
that's wrapped around what I think and what I feel

369
00:14:32,540 --> 00:14:35,900
and I'm going to let my feelings dictate what I want to do

370
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:38,240
and ultimately I'm going to do whatever it is

371
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:41,260
that I want to do as long as it looks good,

372
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:43,760
tastes good, smells good, sounds good, feels good.

373
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:45,200
I'm going to do it without boundaries

374
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,680
and without limitations.

375
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:48,360
And not only am I going to do it,

376
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:51,880
but I'm going to encourage other people to do it as well.

377
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:54,440
And what I missed growing up in this passage

378
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:57,760
was that the tree of the knowledge of good and evil

379
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:59,720
was actually a really good thing.

380
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:05,040
I grew up, I think, just naturally reading

381
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:06,640
because God told them not to eat of it,

382
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:07,900
that it must have been a bad thing,

383
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:09,340
but we know from the Scriptures

384
00:15:09,340 --> 00:15:11,480
that it's actually a good and beautiful thing.

385
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:12,200
Eve saw it.

386
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,800
She saw the fruit and looked delicious.

387
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:15,240
The tree was beautiful.

388
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:17,480
The tree was a good thing.

389
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:20,020
It was just good within the boundaries and context

390
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,780
that God had placed it.

391
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:24,560
See, the tree served an important purpose.

392
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:27,160
It was placed there to give Adam and Eve

393
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:29,920
the opportunity to take God at His word.

394
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:32,800
The tree was good and beautiful,

395
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:35,940
but it was only good within the context

396
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:37,920
that God created it to be.

397
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:42,980
And I think sometimes in our culture today,

398
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:44,800
one of the reasons we see people walking away

399
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:47,940
from their faith is they see something that looks good,

400
00:15:47,940 --> 00:15:51,140
that makes them feel good, that they want to pursue.

401
00:15:51,140 --> 00:15:53,720
And even though God might say something different about it,

402
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:55,660
they're like, well, it's the eye test, right?

403
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:57,100
It's like, I don't care what God says.

404
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:59,020
Maybe I'm misinterpreting what God says.

405
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:01,780
Let's go back to the text and let's study it again.

406
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:05,700
And hopefully I can come out with another understanding

407
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:06,200
of the text.

408
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:08,080
And a lot of this, guys, if I'm being honest,

409
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:10,320
I see a lot of, this isn't in my notes, this is extra.

410
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:13,400
I see a lot of deconstruction happening

411
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:16,100
where people are going back to the Bible

412
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:18,060
and asking questions about their faith,

413
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:21,160
motivated by an emotion and a desire

414
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:22,100
that they already have.

415
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:24,560
And so they're not actually letting the text

416
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:27,720
be the ultimate authority for their life,

417
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:29,000
like we talked about a couple weeks ago.

418
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,260
They come to the text with an answer

419
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,160
that they already want.

420
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:33,760
They say, I have this question.

421
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:35,980
I have what I want the answer to be.

422
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:38,300
And guys, the Bible's big enough

423
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:41,340
that if you go to it with the outcome

424
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:44,380
that you already want, you can really make it say

425
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:45,300
what you want it to say.

426
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:47,180
And I think the rebellious heart says,

427
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:49,120
I see this thing, I want it,

428
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,040
and I'm going to make God say that it's OK.

429
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:55,780
Man, we live in a culture that regularly

430
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:56,920
preaches this to us.

431
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:59,380
If it looks good, tastes good, smells good,

432
00:16:59,380 --> 00:17:01,500
sounds good, feels good, then it must be good.

433
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:03,700
Pursue it, chase after it.

434
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:06,560
Live in light of your desires.

435
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,320
Do what you want to do.

436
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:10,680
Do what makes you feel good.

437
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:13,900
So I wanted to get really practical with this message.

438
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:17,520
And so as we walk through each of these

439
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:19,960
conditional theologies, I wanted to talk about

440
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:22,320
four categories that I see this play out.

441
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:24,140
And I think we'll have a good time

442
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:25,100
talking about these things.

443
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:27,700
Because we're going to talk about sex, money,

444
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:29,540
food, and entertainment.

445
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:32,140
Sex, money, food, entertainment.

446
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:35,380
These are all things that we love to talk about, right?

447
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:37,340
So here's what I see happening

448
00:17:37,340 --> 00:17:41,100
in the conditional theology of the rebellious heart.

449
00:17:43,100 --> 00:17:46,060
That sex is a good thing.

450
00:17:46,060 --> 00:17:47,440
And so we see that.

451
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:48,020
We look at that.

452
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:50,920
We say, if sex is good, then I must be able to enjoy it

453
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:53,420
and participate in whatever way I want.

454
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:55,160
But the reality is sex is good.

455
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:58,060
It's just not good outside of the covenant of marriage.

456
00:17:58,060 --> 00:18:01,340
And it's not a good God inside of the covenant of marriage.

457
00:18:01,340 --> 00:18:03,740
And then we have money, right?

458
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:05,280
Money is a good thing.

459
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:09,580
But the love of money is the root of all evil.

460
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:11,040
Food is a good thing.

461
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:12,060
Beer is a good thing.

462
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:14,780
Buffalo trace whiskey is good.

463
00:18:14,780 --> 00:18:16,920
But not if we overindulge in it.

464
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:19,940
Not if we chase after it as if it's the thing

465
00:18:19,940 --> 00:18:22,240
to give us satisfaction.

466
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:23,540
Entertainment is good.

467
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:25,640
But not when we let the pursuit of it

468
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:27,740
take over our lives.

469
00:18:30,540 --> 00:18:35,280
Recently, I follow a bunch of people that are proponents of deconstruction.

470
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:42,060
It's helped me think about, and when I say proponents of deconstruction, that sounds bad, right?

471
00:18:42,060 --> 00:18:46,360
Because we've said from this series that we are proponents of a healthy deconstruction process.

472
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:53,700
Because really, at the heart of deconstruction, you're just asking questions to solidify what you believe about your faith.

473
00:18:53,780 --> 00:18:57,320
And so if deconstruction leads to renovation, then that's an excellent thing.

474
00:18:57,320 --> 00:19:01,240
But we're fearful of deconstruction that leads people away from the faith.

475
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:05,740
And I follow a bunch of ex-evangelicals, is what they call themselves.

476
00:19:05,740 --> 00:19:09,360
They've walked away from the church, and they're encouraging other people to do the same.

477
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:19,200
And I saw this one post that was talking about the fact that God doesn't care about sex before marriage.

478
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:21,420
You can do whatever you want in whatever ways you want.

479
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:22,880
God doesn't care.

480
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:25,720
He only cares about sex after you're married.

481
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:28,140
So once you're married, then you should be monogamous.

482
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:31,060
But before marriage, you can do whatever you want to do.

483
00:19:31,060 --> 00:19:32,420
It's this if-then statement.

484
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:36,580
Because sex is good, it looks good, tastes good, smells good, feels good, right?

485
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:42,100
Because it's this good gift from God, then I must be able to pursue it without boundaries or limitations.

486
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:46,600
And this is literally, we think this is a new problem.

487
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:50,200
But it's the same problem that they were facing in the first and second century churches.

488
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:51,360
It's called Gnosticism.

489
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:53,640
It's called, God doesn't care about our bodies.

490
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:54,940
He only cares about our hearts.

491
00:19:54,940 --> 00:19:58,380
So we can do whatever we want in this physical body, and He doesn't care.

492
00:19:58,380 --> 00:20:03,600
As long as we have pure hearts and everything else is going to be okay.

493
00:20:04,220 --> 00:20:06,640
But here's the problem, that doesn't work.

494
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:11,020
And not only does that not work, but the thing that I love so much about God's Word

495
00:20:11,020 --> 00:20:16,480
is that it's this ancient text that ultimately science almost always backs up.

496
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:21,120
See, science often validates God's declared design.

497
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:27,080
As I was reading and studying for this message, I found out about this chemical in the brain

498
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:28,820
called vasopressin.

499
00:20:28,820 --> 00:20:35,360
The brain releases vasopressin, which is a bonding chemical whenever two people have sex.

500
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:41,520
And the purpose of this chemical is that after, or the purpose of this chemical is, it's a bonding chemical.

501
00:20:41,520 --> 00:20:47,420
It's like, it's telling the brain that when sex happens, there should be this bond that happens between this.

502
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:53,120
And really the goal is that the two would become one, that they would form a family,

503
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:56,660
and that they would raise this child in a safe and healthy environment.

504
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:59,700
It makes sense from an evolutionary perspective too, right?

505
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:03,760
Like people should come together in family units and protect their children.

506
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:04,580
But here's what happens.

507
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:09,100
After multiple partners, the chemical begins to no longer be effective.

508
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:17,740
And so it's funny because when I grew up, secular people outside of the Bible that didn't care about faith,

509
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:22,460
that didn't care about Jesus, they used to use science as their total authority.

510
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:27,180
Like science was truth, and we did what science said.

511
00:21:27,180 --> 00:21:36,140
But what I'm seeing nowadays is that the rebellious heart is only using science when it backs up their point.

512
00:21:36,740 --> 00:21:39,420
And so we've got these people who would say they're outside of the faith.

513
00:21:39,420 --> 00:21:42,260
They don't care what God has to say, so they shouldn't care what science has to say.

514
00:21:42,260 --> 00:21:44,120
And they don't care what science has to say either.

515
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:44,360
Why?

516
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:47,320
Because sex tastes good, smells good, feels good, looks good, right?

517
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:49,880
Because it's this thing that's good.

518
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:54,260
And so I want to pursue it, and I don't want anybody to tell me anything else.

519
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:58,120
It feels good, so it can't be wrong.

520
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:00,000
I don't care about what religion says about it.

521
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:01,820
I don't care about what science says about it.

522
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:03,920
I care about what my feelings say about it.

523
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:06,380
I'm going to live my truth.

524
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:07,060
Wow.

525
00:22:07,060 --> 00:22:09,120
Stepping on some toes, right?

526
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:15,640
There is an English, even, an evangelist named John Guest.

527
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:17,940
And I came across this quote this week, too.

528
00:22:17,940 --> 00:22:20,040
I thought it was helpful and impactful.

529
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:26,380
He came to America to preach the gospel, and he went into kind of like a gift shop,

530
00:22:26,440 --> 00:22:32,360
and he saw flags that said, don't tread on me, and he saw signs that said, taxation without

531
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:33,820
representation is theft.

532
00:22:33,820 --> 00:22:39,020
And he kind of got a picture of the American mindset, and he said this.

533
00:22:39,020 --> 00:22:45,620
He said, how can I possibly preach the gospel of the kingdom of God to a people who have a

534
00:22:45,620 --> 00:22:48,240
profound aversion to the sovereign?

535
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:55,040
He was saying, how can I preach the kingdom of a God who declares himself to be king and ruler

536
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:57,380
and have all authority over all creation?

537
00:22:57,380 --> 00:23:01,900
How can I preach that message to these people who don't want anybody to have any authority

538
00:23:01,900 --> 00:23:02,540
over them?

539
00:23:02,540 --> 00:23:08,140
And I think that's ultimately at the heart of this conditional theology of the rebellious

540
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:08,360
heart.

541
00:23:08,360 --> 00:23:10,480
I don't want anybody to tell me what to do.

542
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:14,760
I want to decide for myself what feels good, what looks good, what smells good, what tastes

543
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:15,840
good, and I want to pursue it.

544
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:23,020
And I think this is the root cause of a lot of deconstruction, is we say, well, that thing

545
00:23:23,020 --> 00:23:24,660
doesn't seem like it's hurting anybody.

546
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:28,300
It seems good, feels good, tastes good, smells good.

547
00:23:28,300 --> 00:23:32,620
So let's pursue it, and let's encourage other people to pursue it.

548
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:39,000
So this morning, I just want to ask us to seriously consider where we might be buying into this false

549
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:39,560
theology.

550
00:23:41,080 --> 00:23:46,140
That just because sometimes something feels good, that doesn't mean that God ordained

551
00:23:46,140 --> 00:23:49,040
it for us to pursue without limits or boundaries.

552
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:53,720
God's allowed, God's allowed to give us boundaries around the things that he created.

553
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:58,960
He's allowed to give us structure around the gifts that he's given us.

554
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:00,840
So where are we pursuing that in our own life?

555
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:03,220
And where are we encouraging other people to do it?

556
00:24:04,300 --> 00:24:08,140
Maybe we're going against what we think Scripture says, because we don't want to hurt anybody's

557
00:24:08,140 --> 00:24:08,380
feelings.

558
00:24:08,380 --> 00:24:11,460
We want them to be able to pursue what they think is best for their life.

559
00:24:11,460 --> 00:24:13,880
We want them to live their truth.

560
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:21,140
Guys, as a people who believe that following Jesus is a better way to live, encouraging people

561
00:24:21,140 --> 00:24:29,400
to let them live their truth, I don't think it's ultimately going to lead to their abundant life.

562
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:31,220
And so I just want to challenge us.

563
00:24:31,220 --> 00:24:32,520
Let's think about that.

564
00:24:32,520 --> 00:24:36,440
So we see Adam and Eve, they buy into this conditional theology of rebellion.

565
00:24:36,440 --> 00:24:40,900
Ultimately, what they say is, I don't care what God says.

566
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:41,760
I care what I see.

567
00:24:41,760 --> 00:24:43,840
If it looks good, I'm going to pursue it.

568
00:24:44,840 --> 00:24:50,400
And then in the next chapter over, we see their kids, and one of their kids swings the pendulum

569
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:53,960
pretty hard from rebellion to religion.

570
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:57,520
Let's look in Genesis chapter 4, starting in verse 1.

571
00:24:57,520 --> 00:24:57,760
It says,

572
00:24:57,760 --> 00:25:01,720
Now Adam had sexual relations with his wife Eve, and she became pregnant.

573
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:04,120
When she gave birth to Cain, she said,

574
00:25:04,120 --> 00:25:06,620
With the Lord's help, I have produced a man.

575
00:25:06,620 --> 00:25:11,180
Later, she gave birth to his brother and named him Abel.

576
00:25:11,580 --> 00:25:15,240
When they grew up, Abel became a shepherd while Cain cultivated the ground.

577
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:20,000
When it was time for the harvest, Cain presented some of his crops as a gift to the Lord.

578
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:24,020
Abel also brought a gift, the best of the firstborn lambs from his flock.

579
00:25:24,020 --> 00:25:28,940
The Lord accepted Abel and his gift, but he did not accept Cain and his gift.

580
00:25:28,940 --> 00:25:32,580
This made Cain very angry, and he looked dejected.

581
00:25:32,580 --> 00:25:34,440
Why are you so angry, the Lord asked Cain.

582
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:35,960
Why do you look so dejected?

583
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:39,340
You will be accepted if you do what is right.

584
00:25:39,340 --> 00:25:44,800
But if you refuse to do what is right, then watch out, for sin is crouching at the door,

585
00:25:44,800 --> 00:25:46,020
eager to control you.

586
00:25:46,020 --> 00:25:48,500
But you must subdue it and be its master.

587
00:25:48,500 --> 00:25:50,980
One day, Cain suggested to his brother,

588
00:25:50,980 --> 00:25:52,040
Let's go out in the fields.

589
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:57,840
And while they were in the field, Cain attacked his brother, Abel, and killed him.

590
00:25:57,840 --> 00:26:03,180
So we've got Adam and Eve who buy into this conditional theology of rebellion.

591
00:26:03,180 --> 00:26:06,140
If it looks good, tastes good, smells good, feels good, it must be good,

592
00:26:06,140 --> 00:26:08,560
and I can pursue it without boundaries or limitations.

593
00:26:08,560 --> 00:26:15,400
And then, as often happens, their son, the next generation, swings the pendulum over,

594
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:17,000
and he sees that that didn't work, right?

595
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:19,760
He sees the effects of the rebellion of his parents.

596
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:24,780
He sees that that did not lead to life, that it ultimately led them to being kicked out of

597
00:26:24,780 --> 00:26:27,540
the garden, and this separation between them and God.

598
00:26:27,540 --> 00:26:29,900
And he swings the pendulum back to religion.

599
00:26:29,900 --> 00:26:33,900
I know there's a lot happening in Genesis chapter 4 that we could dive into,

600
00:26:33,900 --> 00:26:39,660
but I really just want to focus on what I think is this conditional theology that Abel's buying into.

601
00:26:39,660 --> 00:26:45,080
He swung the pendulum from the rebellious theology, and now the rebellious theology says,

602
00:26:45,080 --> 00:26:48,700
again, it feels good, so I'm going to pursue it, and then I'll be blessed.

603
00:26:48,700 --> 00:26:55,820
And Cain says, that didn't work, and so now I'm going to bring certain things to God,

604
00:26:55,820 --> 00:26:57,120
and he's going to bless me for that.

605
00:26:57,160 --> 00:26:58,920
So Cain creates this religion.

606
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:02,600
He says, I'm going to bring God the fruits of my harvest.

607
00:27:02,600 --> 00:27:08,320
I'm going to give him these gifts, these plants that I have worked hard to grow and create.

608
00:27:08,320 --> 00:27:13,800
And then because I'm thinking about God, I'm creating these gifts and this worship that

609
00:27:13,800 --> 00:27:15,800
I'm going to give him, then God's going to bless me.

610
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:21,540
And so I believe Cain was creating a conditional system where he could bring to God what was

611
00:27:21,540 --> 00:27:24,280
convenient for him.

612
00:27:24,340 --> 00:27:28,000
Again, he's a farmer, and he brings fruits and produce to God.

613
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,760
It's an easy thing for him to do.

614
00:27:29,760 --> 00:27:35,300
He creates a system where he can bring what's convenient for him and turn it over to God.

615
00:27:35,300 --> 00:27:37,980
And in return, he expects that God will bless him.

616
00:27:37,980 --> 00:27:44,460
This is the conditional theology that the rebellious, or that the religious heart creates.

617
00:27:44,460 --> 00:27:50,280
We create rules that are easy for us to follow and hard for other people to follow.

618
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:53,720
And then we expect God to bless us and curse them.

619
00:27:53,720 --> 00:27:59,900
We expect God to bless us for obeying these rules that he never asked us to obey.

620
00:27:59,900 --> 00:28:05,500
We created this system, and we want him to bless us, and we want him to curse other people for

621
00:28:05,500 --> 00:28:08,840
not obeying these rules that he never commanded to begin with.

622
00:28:08,840 --> 00:28:16,040
I think many of us have created a religious system that's somewhat easy and convenient for us to follow.

623
00:28:16,040 --> 00:28:22,240
And we're going to continue to follow it as long as it works out, as long as God gives us in response

624
00:28:22,240 --> 00:28:23,940
what we think we deserve.

625
00:28:23,940 --> 00:28:29,520
But what happens the moment when God stops giving us what we think we want?

626
00:28:29,660 --> 00:28:34,400
Cain thought God was going to bless him for this offering, and instead, God says,

627
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:35,380
I never asked you for that.

628
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:35,980
I don't want that.

629
00:28:35,980 --> 00:28:37,140
That's not what I want from you.

630
00:28:37,140 --> 00:28:39,340
And Cain goes on a killing spree.

631
00:28:39,340 --> 00:28:43,660
He kills his brother because he didn't get from God what he thought he should get.

632
00:28:43,660 --> 00:28:45,660
He created this offering, this system.

633
00:28:45,660 --> 00:28:49,140
I'm going to bring God these things, and in return, God's going to bless me.

634
00:28:49,140 --> 00:28:51,120
God never created that system.

635
00:28:51,120 --> 00:28:53,400
That was a system that Cain created.

636
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:54,300
And we do this.

637
00:28:54,300 --> 00:28:59,720
We make up our own religion, and we expect God to give us in return what we think we deserve.

638
00:28:59,720 --> 00:29:03,740
This is the conditional heart of the religious heart.

639
00:29:03,740 --> 00:29:09,200
So let's unpack how that works out in these four categories we were talking about earlier.

640
00:29:09,200 --> 00:29:12,340
The religious heart says about sex,

641
00:29:12,340 --> 00:29:16,780
I'll be a virgin until marriage, and then God will give me a perfect marriage

642
00:29:16,780 --> 00:29:19,180
and a perfect sex life inside my marriage.

643
00:29:19,180 --> 00:29:21,120
We create this religious system.

644
00:29:21,120 --> 00:29:23,260
We expect God to give us something in return.

645
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:27,440
Money, I'll give God 10% of my money, and he will bless me financially.

646
00:29:27,440 --> 00:29:32,320
Food, I won't drink alcohol, and God will bless me with a long and healthy life.

647
00:29:32,320 --> 00:29:36,460
Entertainment, I'm going to make sure that my family only consumes Christian content,

648
00:29:36,460 --> 00:29:38,920
and God will bless me with a perfect family.

649
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:41,980
But what happens when this doesn't work out?

650
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:45,180
Guys, this is not a system that God promised.

651
00:29:45,180 --> 00:29:48,040
And we're pushing this system on people.

652
00:29:48,040 --> 00:29:49,920
We're preaching this message to people.

653
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:57,220
I grew up in what evangelical people my age would call the I-kiss-dating-goodbye generation.

654
00:29:57,220 --> 00:30:03,860
Because there was this book and conference and all of this idea about getting rid of dating,

655
00:30:03,860 --> 00:30:07,640
no kissing, no holding hands, no dating, no anything until marriage.

656
00:30:07,640 --> 00:30:11,640
You're going to do this biblical courtship, and then you'll get married.

657
00:30:11,740 --> 00:30:17,440
And all in one day, all of a sudden, you'll go from not having any sex to having the best sex of your life.

658
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:20,280
And we were taught that that's what God promised us.

659
00:30:20,280 --> 00:30:21,340
And guys, guess what happened?

660
00:30:21,340 --> 00:30:23,600
It didn't work out, right?

661
00:30:23,600 --> 00:30:29,260
Some of us, God called us to a season of singleness, and we're doing everything that we thought we should be doing,

662
00:30:29,360 --> 00:30:31,600
and God's not giving up His end of the bargain.

663
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:35,600
Some of us, we did what we thought we were supposed to do,

664
00:30:35,600 --> 00:30:39,900
and then sex didn't work out as well as we thought it was going to because we never talked about it.

665
00:30:39,900 --> 00:30:42,140
We were never taught about it in a good light.

666
00:30:42,140 --> 00:30:44,460
And so it became this dark secret.

667
00:30:44,460 --> 00:30:46,720
Some of us, we did the right thing.

668
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:52,020
And then maybe we found out later in our marriage that our spouse was actually addicted to pornography

669
00:30:52,020 --> 00:30:57,980
because they had all of this built-up frustration and tension about what He's being taught in church about sexuality.

670
00:30:57,980 --> 00:31:03,800
And so we create this religion, and then we don't get the results that we thought God was going to give us

671
00:31:03,800 --> 00:31:05,840
because God never promised that to begin with.

672
00:31:05,840 --> 00:31:07,300
It's a system that we created.

673
00:31:07,300 --> 00:31:11,660
It's a conditional statement that we put on God that He never asked for us.

674
00:31:11,660 --> 00:31:15,580
Money, what happens if you tithe faithfully?

675
00:31:15,580 --> 00:31:17,100
You lose your job.

676
00:31:17,100 --> 00:31:21,260
You can't provide for your family the way that you thought you would be able to.

677
00:31:21,260 --> 00:31:26,700
What happens when you don't drink, you don't smoke, you don't do any of those bad things,

678
00:31:26,700 --> 00:31:28,420
and then you get the cancer diagnosis?

679
00:31:28,420 --> 00:31:33,940
Meanwhile, your neighbor down the street who smokes a pack a day and gets drunk every night

680
00:31:33,940 --> 00:31:35,820
is living a healthy and happy life.

681
00:31:35,820 --> 00:31:39,640
What happens to your heart when you believe a false theology?

682
00:31:39,640 --> 00:31:45,080
You get angry, and you get mad, and you blame God, and you walk away from your faith

683
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:48,960
because you bought a religion that God never sold you.

684
00:31:48,960 --> 00:31:50,440
Some preacher might have sold it to you.

685
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:54,280
Some church might have sold it to you, but it wasn't God's vision for your life.

686
00:31:54,280 --> 00:31:58,780
And I see so many people that are walking away from the church, and I get it.

687
00:31:58,780 --> 00:32:02,540
They're hurt because some preacher taught them something that isn't true,

688
00:32:02,540 --> 00:32:07,040
handed them a conditional religious theology that was never from God.

689
00:32:07,040 --> 00:32:09,280
Entertainment.

690
00:32:09,280 --> 00:32:11,500
We're going to only consume Christian content.

691
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:16,540
But then what happens when you raise your kids up in what you think is the right way,

692
00:32:16,540 --> 00:32:18,840
and they end up walking away from the faith?

693
00:32:18,840 --> 00:32:24,180
I had a professor in college that said, the Bible verse that says, you reap what you sow,

694
00:32:24,180 --> 00:32:29,060
that that Bible verse is a promise that if you are godly, your kids will be godly.

695
00:32:29,060 --> 00:32:35,100
He said it was 100% guarantee, and now his son has walked away from the church.

696
00:32:35,100 --> 00:32:40,800
And so what happens when we buy this life, when a preacher tells us that if you're a godly person,

697
00:32:40,800 --> 00:32:46,400
and if you raise your family around godly entertainment, that they will become godly.

698
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:49,000
And then what happens when your kids walk away from the faith?

699
00:32:49,080 --> 00:32:51,360
Again, our hearts are broken.

700
00:32:51,360 --> 00:32:52,080
We're angry.

701
00:32:52,080 --> 00:32:53,860
We lash out.

702
00:32:53,860 --> 00:32:55,720
And that's what Cain does.

703
00:32:55,720 --> 00:32:57,380
He created this system.

704
00:32:57,380 --> 00:33:01,020
He brought these offerings to God, and he thought, in turn, God would bless him.

705
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:06,200
And then when God wasn't happy with his offerings or his blessings, they got furious.

706
00:33:06,200 --> 00:33:11,220
He got furious, and he ended up killing his brother.

707
00:33:11,220 --> 00:33:18,480
So the problem with these religious conditional theology is that we put our trust in ideas and concepts

708
00:33:18,480 --> 00:33:21,660
that God never asked us to trust in.

709
00:33:21,660 --> 00:33:27,300
And then when God doesn't hold up his end of the deal that he never agreed upon,

710
00:33:27,300 --> 00:33:28,920
we go on a killing spree.

711
00:33:28,920 --> 00:33:31,900
So if the sex thing didn't work out the way that we thought it would,

712
00:33:31,900 --> 00:33:35,780
we go and we sell ourselves short to a cheap pornography addiction.

713
00:33:35,780 --> 00:33:38,920
When the financial stuff didn't work out the way that we thought it should,

714
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:40,860
we go into crazy amounts of credit card debt.

715
00:33:40,860 --> 00:33:43,520
We buy whatever we want to make ourselves feel better.

716
00:33:43,520 --> 00:33:47,780
When the health thing doesn't work out, we turn to gluttony and to drunkenness.

717
00:33:47,780 --> 00:33:51,260
When the entertainment thing doesn't work out, we pursue laziness.

718
00:33:51,260 --> 00:33:59,620
We get so mad at God because we put this religious system on him that he never asked us to do.

719
00:33:59,620 --> 00:34:01,360
We give him this conditional theology.

720
00:34:01,360 --> 00:34:04,720
If I bring these things to you, then you give me these things back.

721
00:34:05,380 --> 00:34:09,500
And God doesn't play by those rules because that's not the gospel.

722
00:34:09,500 --> 00:34:17,200
And this often leads to us religious people swinging the pendulum back towards rebellion.

723
00:34:17,200 --> 00:34:19,520
And it's a pendulum that goes back and forth.

724
00:34:20,060 --> 00:34:30,540
People who grew up in secular homes, their childhoods were ruined because their parents were alcoholics and substance abusers.

725
00:34:30,540 --> 00:34:33,620
They find hope and healing in the church.

726
00:34:33,620 --> 00:34:34,980
And then they turn to religion.

727
00:34:34,980 --> 00:34:37,060
And they try and raise their kids in a religious home.

728
00:34:37,060 --> 00:34:39,420
And their kids follow all the rules.

729
00:34:39,420 --> 00:34:41,800
And then things don't work out the way that they thought it would.

730
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:44,340
And they swing the pendulum back to rebellion.

731
00:34:44,340 --> 00:34:46,500
And this happens over and over again.

732
00:34:46,500 --> 00:34:52,920
And I think it's a huge contributing factor to so many people deconstructing their faith.

733
00:34:52,920 --> 00:34:57,300
Because they've bought the lie of these two false conditional theologies.

734
00:34:58,780 --> 00:35:02,760
They've bought the lie that if it looks good, tastes good, smells good, feels good,

735
00:35:02,760 --> 00:35:04,760
they should be able to pursue it without boundary or limit.

736
00:35:04,760 --> 00:35:11,260
Or they've bought the lie that I'm going to bring God these offerings and he's going to bless me in return.

737
00:35:11,260 --> 00:35:15,220
And neither of those things are the true gospel.

738
00:35:15,220 --> 00:35:21,720
Rebellion says I can become God by deciding for myself what is good and bad based on my feelings,

739
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:22,860
what I think, what I see.

740
00:35:22,860 --> 00:35:24,440
I don't care what God says.

741
00:35:24,440 --> 00:35:26,040
I care what I see.

742
00:35:27,360 --> 00:35:32,540
And religion says I can control God by creating a reward system that he has to honor.

743
00:35:32,540 --> 00:35:35,580
But what if there's another way?

744
00:35:35,580 --> 00:35:39,380
I'm going to wrap up by turning to Matthew chapter 4.

745
00:35:39,380 --> 00:35:44,720
Matthew chapter 4, we see Jesus, not in a garden, but in a desert.

746
00:35:44,720 --> 00:35:50,720
And the same enemy that came to Adam and Eve and offered them a conditional theology

747
00:35:50,720 --> 00:35:53,260
comes to Jesus and offers him a conditional theology.

748
00:35:53,860 --> 00:36:00,240
In verse 8, Satan's offered Jesus a couple of different things and it comes to a head at verse 8.

749
00:36:00,240 --> 00:36:07,180
It says, next, the devil took Jesus to the peak of a very high mountain and showed him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory.

750
00:36:07,180 --> 00:36:12,000
I will give it all to you, he said, if you will kneel down and worship me.

751
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:15,440
Satan says, the enemy says, I'll give you everything.

752
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:17,920
You can have all the kingdoms of the world.

753
00:36:17,920 --> 00:36:19,940
All you have to do is bow down and worship me.

754
00:36:20,020 --> 00:36:21,360
Jesus says, get out of here, Satan.

755
00:36:21,360 --> 00:36:27,220
For the Scripture says, you must worship the Lord your God and serve him only.

756
00:36:27,220 --> 00:36:32,400
Then the devil went away and the angels came and took care of Jesus.

757
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:40,940
See, we have a very real enemy that regularly offers us false conditional theologies.

758
00:36:40,940 --> 00:36:49,220
He tries to convince the rebellious heart that they can control God by creating their own rules

759
00:36:49,220 --> 00:36:51,620
and that if they follow those rules, God will bless them.

760
00:36:51,620 --> 00:36:53,860
Or he offers the rebellious heart.

761
00:36:53,860 --> 00:36:56,060
Just chase after what you feel.

762
00:36:56,060 --> 00:37:00,140
Pursue the things that look good, taste good, smell good, without boundary or limitation.

763
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:04,220
And that will lead to a satisfied life.

764
00:37:04,220 --> 00:37:07,000
And Jesus was faced with the same temptation.

765
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:12,440
Adam and Eve had a perfect opportunity to say no to this temptation.

766
00:37:12,440 --> 00:37:14,840
They were in a garden with everything that they could ever want.

767
00:37:14,840 --> 00:37:20,140
Jesus, after 40 days of being in the wilderness and fasting, has offered the same thing.

768
00:37:20,140 --> 00:37:20,940
You can have it all.

769
00:37:20,940 --> 00:37:23,540
All you have to do is bow down and worship me.

770
00:37:23,540 --> 00:37:27,640
Say yes to this temptation and receive temporary blessing.

771
00:37:29,140 --> 00:37:32,120
But if you do, you'll be separated from your father.

772
00:37:32,120 --> 00:37:38,580
Or take God at his word and receive eternal reward.

773
00:37:38,580 --> 00:37:43,120
And Jesus succeeds where Adam and Eve fail.

774
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:45,920
Jesus succeeds where all of us have failed.

775
00:37:45,920 --> 00:37:50,140
He chooses to be obedient to the one true command.

776
00:37:50,140 --> 00:37:54,840
You must worship the Lord your God and serve him only.

777
00:37:55,040 --> 00:37:59,360
See, the message of the gospel of Jesus, it is a conditional message.

778
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:03,220
But it's not the condition of rebellion or the condition of religion.

779
00:38:03,220 --> 00:38:07,600
It's based on the condition of faith and submission to Jesus.

780
00:38:07,600 --> 00:38:12,420
The gospel is conditional in that Jesus succeeds in every way that we have failed.

781
00:38:12,420 --> 00:38:17,180
And he offers his success freely to us by us accepting it by faith.

782
00:38:17,260 --> 00:38:22,120
By obeying this command to worship the Lord our God and to serve him only.

783
00:38:22,120 --> 00:38:28,640
The entire faith renovation process comes down to our willingness to obey this one command.

784
00:38:30,080 --> 00:38:37,020
Are we willing to worship the Lord our God and serve him only?

785
00:38:37,020 --> 00:38:39,420
All of it comes down to that.

786
00:38:39,420 --> 00:38:41,060
This is the heart of the father.

787
00:38:41,060 --> 00:38:45,740
We've said the whole goal of the deconstruction process is to get us back to the heart of the father.

788
00:38:45,740 --> 00:38:51,800
The heart of the father is that we would worship the Lord our God and serve him only.

789
00:38:52,460 --> 00:38:59,460
If we start our deconstruction process here with this command, and then we ask questions about our faith,

790
00:38:59,460 --> 00:39:01,800
we ask questions about the religion that we've been handed,

791
00:39:01,800 --> 00:39:05,880
we ask questions about the things that look good, taste good, smell good, how should we pursue them?

792
00:39:05,880 --> 00:39:10,780
If we do that all under the banner of we're going to worship the Lord our God and serve him only,

793
00:39:10,780 --> 00:39:15,140
I promise that we might come to different conclusions about secondary issues,

794
00:39:15,140 --> 00:39:17,440
but if we're willing to unite around this command,

795
00:39:17,440 --> 00:39:20,640
that we're going to worship God and serve him only,

796
00:39:20,680 --> 00:39:23,380
I promise we can find unity around that.

797
00:39:23,380 --> 00:39:32,680
So I want to end by having us think through what conditional theology are we most inclined to this morning?

798
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:36,160
Are you most inclined to the rebellious theology?

799
00:39:36,160 --> 00:39:37,260
You don't want to miss out.

800
00:39:37,260 --> 00:39:40,380
You see things that look good, taste good, smell good, feel good,

801
00:39:40,380 --> 00:39:44,140
and you want to pursue it, or you at least want other people to be able to pursue it.

802
00:39:44,140 --> 00:39:48,960
Or maybe you're trusting in some man-made religious system.

803
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:50,140
Maybe it's been handed to you.

804
00:39:50,140 --> 00:39:52,620
Maybe you accepted it because you thought it was the gospel,

805
00:39:52,620 --> 00:39:56,500
and you thought if you did these things the right way, then God would bless you.

806
00:39:56,500 --> 00:40:03,240
Or maybe you're like me, and I feel like I have swung the pendulum a few times in my life.

807
00:40:03,240 --> 00:40:08,240
I feel like sometimes I am in a rebellious state, and I just believe, you know what?

808
00:40:08,240 --> 00:40:09,460
God, I love you.

809
00:40:09,460 --> 00:40:11,180
I want to obey you, but this thing looks good.

810
00:40:11,180 --> 00:40:12,040
This thing tastes good.

811
00:40:12,040 --> 00:40:12,940
This thing smells good.

812
00:40:12,940 --> 00:40:13,740
This thing feels good.

813
00:40:13,740 --> 00:40:16,040
I want to pursue it for a while and see what happens.

814
00:40:16,100 --> 00:40:17,260
And it always leaves me empty.

815
00:40:17,260 --> 00:40:22,800
And what happens oftentimes when I'm in rebellion to God is I swing the pendulum and I go to religion.

816
00:40:22,800 --> 00:40:26,960
Rather than submitting to his lordship and coming back to the center and saying,

817
00:40:26,960 --> 00:40:27,980
God, you are Lord.

818
00:40:27,980 --> 00:40:29,460
I want to worship you and serve you only.

819
00:40:29,520 --> 00:40:33,320
I tend to feel bad about my rebellion and go towards religion.

820
00:40:33,320 --> 00:40:41,400
I don't know where you're at this morning, but my challenge for all of us is that we would learn to put to death our conditional theologies,

821
00:40:41,400 --> 00:40:47,980
that we would learn to trust the way of Jesus, that we would worship the Lord our God and serve him only,

822
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:53,160
even if it doesn't lead to some things that we want it to lead to.

823
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:54,000
See, here's the deal.

824
00:40:54,000 --> 00:41:00,520
Jesus promises that if we'll do this, he promises what he calls abundant life.

825
00:41:00,520 --> 00:41:03,020
But abundant life doesn't always mean earthly blessings.

826
00:41:03,020 --> 00:41:05,000
It doesn't mean that everything goes well.

827
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:10,120
It doesn't mean that we get everything that we want to get or that our life ends up looking the way that it wants to end up looking.

828
00:41:10,120 --> 00:41:16,100
But it means that our life is fulfilled and satisfied because we're living for eternal purposes.

829
00:41:16,100 --> 00:41:19,940
We're going to reap eternal benefits.

830
00:41:19,940 --> 00:41:22,320
So let's get real practical.

831
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:23,860
I know I'm over time.

832
00:41:23,860 --> 00:41:27,800
Let's get real practical about what this looks like with those four categories.

833
00:41:27,800 --> 00:41:32,560
If we're worshiping the Lord God and serving him only, sex, we view it as a gift from God,

834
00:41:32,560 --> 00:41:37,820
and we will enjoy it within the parameters that he has defined, and we will not worship it.

835
00:41:37,820 --> 00:41:39,180
Sex is not a God.

836
00:41:39,180 --> 00:41:39,780
It's a gift.

837
00:41:40,540 --> 00:41:40,780
Money.

838
00:41:40,780 --> 00:41:47,820
Everything that I have is a gift from God, and I will use everything I have to serve the least of these

839
00:41:47,820 --> 00:41:49,500
and build God's kingdom, not our own.

840
00:41:49,500 --> 00:41:53,020
James says true religion is taking care of the widow and the orphan.

841
00:41:53,020 --> 00:41:56,940
We're going to use everything we have to serve the least of these to build God's kingdom.

842
00:41:56,940 --> 00:41:57,320
Food.

843
00:41:57,320 --> 00:42:04,880
I will use food to fuel my body in a healthy way, and my dinner table to invest in relationships with people for the glory of God.

844
00:42:04,880 --> 00:42:09,720
I'm going to use food to bring people around to build relationships that I can point people to Jesus

845
00:42:09,720 --> 00:42:11,180
and build his kingdom entertainment.

846
00:42:11,180 --> 00:42:18,260
I will enjoy the good gift from God in their proper context, and I will use them as an opportunity to worship him.

847
00:42:18,260 --> 00:42:23,980
Let's be a people who reject the false conditions of rebellion and religion,

848
00:42:23,980 --> 00:42:29,160
and let's be a people who intentionally learn to take God at his word no matter where it leads us,

849
00:42:29,160 --> 00:42:35,100
because we truly believe that following Jesus is a better way.

850
00:42:35,100 --> 00:42:35,620
Let's pray.

851
00:42:35,620 --> 00:42:38,900
Father, I know we covered a lot today.

852
00:42:38,900 --> 00:42:44,860
I pray, Holy Spirit, that you would take all of the information that we communicated this morning

853
00:42:44,860 --> 00:42:49,620
and that you would speak directly to each individual what we need to hear.

854
00:42:49,620 --> 00:42:56,080
Challenge us, convict us, encourage us, and point us back to you.

855
00:42:56,080 --> 00:43:00,940
And I pray that as people wrestle with this process of deconstruction and the questions that they have,

856
00:43:00,940 --> 00:43:06,920
that we would create a community at Canvas where it's a safe and healthy place for people to wrestle with questions,

857
00:43:06,920 --> 00:43:10,520
for people to be angry about the religion that they bought,

858
00:43:10,520 --> 00:43:13,760
that they were sold from some preacher, some pastor, some church,

859
00:43:13,760 --> 00:43:16,680
that they'd be allowed to be angry about those things,

860
00:43:16,680 --> 00:43:21,560
and that they would mourn those things and find hope and healing in Jesus,

861
00:43:21,560 --> 00:43:28,600
and that those who are chasing after what their heart desires and what they feel looks good, tastes good, smells good,

862
00:43:28,600 --> 00:43:34,120
I pray that they would be able to realize that they bought a lie that will never satisfy them.

863
00:43:34,120 --> 00:43:36,360
It might feel good in the moment, but it will not satisfy them.

864
00:43:36,360 --> 00:43:44,740
And I pray that they would find hope and healing in this command to love the Lord your God with all of your heart, soul, mind, and strength.

865
00:43:44,740 --> 00:43:48,040
To worship the Lord your God and serve Him only.

866
00:43:48,040 --> 00:43:51,580
I pray all of us in Jesus' name. Amen.

867
00:43:51,580 --> 00:43:54,360
Thank you for checking out Canvas today.

868
00:43:54,360 --> 00:43:58,840
Canvas is a church of real people with real lives simply learning to follow Jesus.

869
00:43:58,840 --> 00:44:01,800
And we truly hope that you were encouraged by today's message.

870
00:44:01,800 --> 00:44:05,400
My name is Michelle Meeks, and I'm the children's pastor here at Canvas.

871
00:44:05,740 --> 00:44:10,460
If you're new to Canvas or you'd like to get more connected, we have several ways that you can do so.

872
00:44:10,460 --> 00:44:14,340
You can go to our website at canvaswinchester.org,

873
00:44:14,340 --> 00:44:20,140
or you can download our app if you'd like notifications about what is going on daily and weekly here at Canvas

874
00:44:20,140 --> 00:44:24,320
by searching Canvas Church Winchester in your app store.

875
00:44:24,320 --> 00:44:27,920
We also have social media pages and a YouTube channel,

876
00:44:27,920 --> 00:44:30,820
which will house all of the videos that you see here today,

877
00:44:30,820 --> 00:44:34,260
as well as my personal favorite Canvas Kids videos.

878
00:44:34,860 --> 00:44:41,680
If you would like to give financially to Canvas, you can do so at going to canvaswinchester.org backslash give.

879
00:44:41,680 --> 00:44:43,240
That's all I have for you.

880
00:44:43,240 --> 00:44:44,880
I hope you have a great rest of your day.
